HyperPrecision.jl is a Julia port and reimplementation based on the method
described in the following paper:

  Sumit Banik and Souvik Bera,
  "HyperPrecision: A Mathematica package for High-Precision Numerical
  Evaluation of Multivariate Hypergeometric Functions",
  arXiv:2605.30216.

The Mathematica reference implementation is available at

  https://github.com/HyperPrecision/HyperPrecision

and identifies Sumit Banik and Souvik Bera as its authors. The reference
implementation is distributed under version 3 of the GNU General Public
License. This repository does not include the Mathematica source files.

The Julia implementation and its modifications are recorded in this
repository from August 15, 2026. HyperPrecision.jl is distributed under
version 3 of the GNU General Public License, with no option to use a later
version. See LICENSE for the complete terms.
